{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01TO", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$A \\to B \\to C$", "MATH_0002": "$A \\to C$", "MATH_0003": "$A \\to B$", "MATH_0004": "$B \\to C$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-locally-finite-presentation-characterize}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-compose-finite-type}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-compose-after-separated}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-quasi-compact-permanence}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8c4b9f95304ea02b960b9db1caedfa6391a7a8b88024501779730234b404ea6b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4b68c8c81bf2996af6c7a4019ec315e32507faee223a1547d7853155348c3714", "source_text": "Proof of (1). Via Lemma <REF_0001>\nthis translates into the following algebra\nfact: Given ring maps <MATH_0001> such that <MATH_0002> is\nof finite presentation and <MATH_0003> is of finite type,\nthen <MATH_0004> is of finite presentation. See\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0002>.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nPart (2) follows from (1) and\nSchemes, Lemmas <REF_0003> and\n<REF_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3e223ce291f2b2b5af5e8ebed55d445cac81331e12eaa913fb9640b317d507ca", "unit_id": "tag:02FV:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01TO", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Delta : X \\to X \\times_Y X$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Delta$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Delta$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-diagonal-morphism-finite-type}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:26aaaf1149b743f8a27c6337f5f098e1a4596f6f5aee669f26aab2ff36c69efd", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e66f9fc8eac8e508393ab06789bcd4568ec4f35f12bb5406c7da5234873cb52b", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes with diagonal\n<MATH_0002>. If <MATH_0003> is locally of finite type\nthen <MATH_0004> is locally of finite presentation. If <MATH_0005> is quasi-separated\nand locally of finite type, then <MATH_0006> is of finite presentation.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4753c0f1ffe360df3ccefd2c80f6e4f471b98b19df2ccab937c1507ab4ff1f9c", "unit_id": "tag:0818:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01TO", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Delta$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$X \\times_Y X \\to X$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "MATH_0006": "$X$", "MATH_0007": "$X \\times_Y X$", "MATH_0008": "$X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-finite-type}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-finite-presentation-permanence}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-monomorphism-separated}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c9fd9ca5faaef1aae60de69d163129ee3fd86062d9d2bf2d4a6307e2bb01a1d6", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a8836fd0988eec71d5271ee88c8615f2faf757ad1edbd65da577b30272183c82", "source_text": "Note that <MATH_0001> is a morphism of schemes over <MATH_0002> (via the second\nprojection <MATH_0003>). Assume <MATH_0004> is locally of finite type.\nNote that <MATH_0005> is of finite presentation over <MATH_0006> and <MATH_0007> is\nlocally of finite type over <MATH_0008> (by Lemma <REF_0001>).\nThus the first statement holds by\nLemma <REF_0002>.\nThe second statement follows from the first, the definitions, and\nthe fact that a diagonal morphism is a monomorphism, hence separated\n(Schemes, Lemma <REF_0003>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:98fc08b6c2023ae13f7c7a3c4c2859660d75d18335e45169d66cbe5b47b46692", "unit_id": "tag:0818:proof"}
